{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The short Ethernet cables fit my recent networking purchases and interest in keeping connections tidy; they serve a different purpose from the longer cables I already have.",
    "The powered USB hub feels useful alongside my keyboard and adapters because it could organize several accessories and let me switch them individually. The SATA dock also fits my computer interests, though I would need a spare drive before choosing it."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo speakers, smart displays, and Fire TV Stick do not help with my current computer and Raspberry Pi setup; buying electronics does not mean I am looking to add voice assistants or streaming devices.",
    "The HDMI cable repeats a need I have already covered, while the 4TB SSD assumes a storage upgrade I have not indicated. The Fire TV Ethernet adapter also serves a device I have not shown a need for."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in computer accessories seems to have been stretched into interest in household electronics generally.",
    "Having bought cables and memory cards seems to have been taken as a reason to offer more cables and much larger storage, without considering whether they solve a new problem."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent Ethernet adapter, cable purchases, headphone mount, and cleaning equipment suggest I am maintaining and organizing an existing setup.",
    "Compatibility and an immediate use matter to me: a hub can support accessories I already use, but a SATA dock needs a spare drive and a Fire TV adapter needs a relevant device."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in practical computer accessories but missed my current focus on organizing and maintaining equipment I already use."
}"}
